0003: build xnu-12377's PPL-era machine layer for SWEET (config_pmap_ppl).

In 12377 osfmk/conf/files.arm64 builds arm_init.c, arm_vm_init.c and start.s only with config_pmap_ppl (Macs moved
to SPTM, so 12377's MacOSX config, which MASTER.arm64.sweet is based on, dropped it). Without them build 7 linked
with 59 undefined symbols (__start, BootArgs, gPhysBase, phystokv, bootstrap_pagetables, vm_kernel_slide, ...).
The 8796 SWEET config had config_pmap_ppl too. It does not turn the PPL monitor on: XNU_MONITOR is only defined in
Apple's own board blocks in board_config.h, never for SWEET.

--- a/config/MASTER.arm64.sweet
+++ b/config/MASTER.arm64.sweet
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 #else
 #  ARM_EXTRAS_BASE = [ config_pmap_ppl ]
 #endif
-#  KERNEL_BASE =    [ arm64 medium msgb_large config_requires_u32_munging config_delay_idle_sleep config_proc_udata_storage config_uexc config_darkboot nos_arm_asm nos_arm_pmap ]
+#  KERNEL_BASE =    [ arm64 medium msgb_large config_requires_u32_munging config_delay_idle_sleep config_proc_udata_storage config_uexc config_darkboot config_pmap_ppl nos_arm_asm nos_arm_pmap ]
 #  KERNEL_RELEASE = [ KERNEL_BASE release ]
 #  KERNEL_DEV =     [ KERNEL_BASE development mach_assert config_xnupost proc_ref_debug config_proc_resource_limits config_ext_paniclog ]
 #  KERNEL_DEBUG =   [ KERNEL_BASE debug mach_assert config_xnupost config_waitq_stats config_workloop_debug config_proc_resource_limits config_ext_paniclog ]
